1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,550
Support answers from each business's own
knowledge, kept strictly apart.

2
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:08,450
This is a multi-tenant AI customer support
platform.

3
00:00:08,700 --> 00:00:11,950
One business gets a dashboard, a knowledge
base,

4
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:15,150
an embeddable chat widget

5
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:18,950
and a shared team inbox.

6
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:23,950
Documents move from queued to ready in the
background.

7
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:25,590
Answers carry their sources.

8
00:00:25,640 --> 00:00:28,950
The reply is a fixed demo sentence, but
the retrieval is real.

9
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:32,412
A second business cannot open this
workspace.

10
00:00:32,462 --> 00:00:34,950
It gets organization not found.

11
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:39,150
A visitor's conversation survives a
reload.

12
00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:43,150
Analytics come from recorded events,

13
00:00:43,700 --> 00:00:47,950
and installing the widget twice still
keeps one.

14
00:00:48,400 --> 00:00:50,493
Underneath are four layers:

15
00:00:50,543 --> 00:00:54,421
the experience layer, the application,
data and background processing,

16
00:00:54,471 --> 00:00:56,207
and retrieval intelligence.

17
00:00:56,257 --> 00:01:00,850
It is one modular monolith running as
several processes in containers,

18
00:01:00,900 --> 00:01:03,350
not a set of microservices.

19
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:11,073
The first audit passed five hundred and
eighty-two backend tests and still found

20
00:01:11,123 --> 00:01:12,599
seven problems.

21
00:01:12,649 --> 00:01:17,559
All seven now pass locally, across fifteen
hundred and five tests.

22
00:01:17,609 --> 00:01:21,756
Real AI quality and production readiness
are still unproven.

23
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:26,950
Software engineering, full-stack and
applied AI.

24
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:29,550
Case study at venuja dot online.
